---
title: "Statistics for Behavioral Science"
code: "PSY-210"
category: "psychology"
credits: "4"
prerequisites:
  - "2026/PSY-200"
corequisites:
  - "2026/MTH-245"
prerequisiteNote: "Prerequisites: PSY 200"
corequisiteNote: "Corequisite: MTH 245 or equivalent"
---

Introduces the principles and processes of statistics for behavioral science research. Focuses on selection and application of appropriate statistical tests and accurate interpretation of behavioral science data. Utilizes statistical software for conducting statistical analysis. Lecture 4 hours. Total 4 hours per week.
